        "role": "tool",
        "tool_call_id": "call_V8S8fYZBzlOwm6r1wJDgOVlZ",
        "content": "=== np_zap ===\nZap a wand in the given cardinal (n, e, s, w) or ordinal direction (ne, se, sw, nw) or target yourself using self.\n\n=== np_pickup ===\nPickup things at your location or specify where you want to pickup an item.\n\n=== np_up ===\nGo up a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.\n\n=== np_down ===\nGo down a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.\n\n=== np_loot ===\nLoot a box on the floor.\n\n=== np_offer ===\nOffer a sacrifice to the gods.\n\n=== np_drop ===\nDrop an item.\n\n=== np_read ===\nRead a scroll, spellbook, or something else.\n\n=== np_put_on ===\nPut on an accessory.\n\n=== np_remove ===\nRemove an accessory (ring, amulet, or blindfold).\n\n=== np_takeoff ===\nTake off one piece of armor.\n\n=== np_wield ===\nWield a weapon.\n\n=== np_wear ===\nWear a piece of armor.\n\n=== np_apply ===\nApply (use) a tool. If used on a wand, that wand will be broken, releasing its magic in the process.\n\n=== np_eat ===\nEat something from your inventory or straight from the ground.\n\n=== np_drink ===\nDrink something from your inventory or straight from the ground.\n\n=== np_tip ===\nTip out the content of a container.\n\n=== np_dip ===\nDip an object into something.\n\n=== np_kick ===\nKick something.\n\n=== np_rest ===\nRests n-moves while doing nothing or until something happens (default=5).\n\n=== np_cast ===\nOpens your spellbook to cast a spell.\n\n=== np_pay ===\nPay your shopping bill.\n\n=== np_pray ===\nPray to the gods for help.\n\n=== np_look ===\nLook at what is under you.\n\n=== np_set_avoid_monster_flag ===\nIf set to true skills will try to avoid monsters.\n\n=== np_melee_attack ===\nPursues and attacks a given target using melee attacks until it is dead.\n\n=== np_explore_level ===\nExplores the level to find new rooms, as well as hidden doors and corridors.\n\n=== np_move_to ===\nMove to the specified position using pathfinding.\n\n=== np_go_to ===\nMoves to the specified room or corridor using the shortest path possible.\n\n=== np_press_key ===\nPresses the given letter. For special keys only ESC, SPACE, and ENTER are supported.\n\n=== np_type_text ===\nTypes the text by pressing the keys in order.\n\n=== reveal ===\nReveal a rectangular region of the dungeon map as ASCII (for the bounding-box observation mode, where the map is otherwise hidden). Coordinates are map cells: x = column 0-78, y = row 0-20, inclusive.\n\n=== rollback ===\nUndo the last n turns, returning the game to the state it was in before them. Use after a mistake -- walking into a losing fight, triggering a trap, wasting turns in a dead end. Costs one turn and no \n\n",
