      "parent": 6,
      "message": {
        "role": "tool",
        "tool_call_id": "call_ZlnoHuvp61mNrbklB1aefLbd",
        "content": "np_zap - Zap a wand in the given cardinal (n, e, s, w) or ordinal direction (ne, se, sw, nw) or target yourself using self.\n\nnp_pickup - Pickup things at your location or specify where you want to pickup an item.\n\nnp_up - Go up a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.\n\nnp_down - Go down a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.\n\nnp_loot - Loot a box on the floor.\n\nnp_offer - Offer a sacrifice to the gods.\n\nnp_drop - Drop an item.\n\nnp_read - Read a scroll, spellbook, or something else.\n\nnp_put_on - Put on an accessory.\n\nnp_remove - Remove an accessory (ring, amulet, or blindfold).\n\nnp_takeoff - Take off one piece of armor.\n\nnp_wield - Wield a weapon.\n\nnp_wear - Wear a piece of armor.\n\nnp_apply - Apply (use) a tool. If used on a wand, that wand will be broken, releasing its magic in the process.\n\nnp_eat - Eat something from your inventory or straight from the ground.\n\nnp_drink - Drink something from your inventory or straight from the ground.\n\nnp_tip - Tip out the content of a container.\n\nnp_dip - Dip an object into something.\n\nnp_kick - Kick something.\n\nnp_rest - Rests n-moves while doing nothing or until something happens (default=5).\n\nnp_cast - Opens your spellbook to cast a spell.\n\nnp_pay - Pay your shopping bill.\n\nnp_pray - Pray to the gods for help.\n\nnp_look - Look at what is under you.\n\nnp_set_avoid_monster_flag - If set to true skills will try to avoid monsters.\n\nnp_melee_attack - Pursues and attacks a given target using melee attacks until it is dead.\n\nnp_explore_level - Explores the level to find new rooms, as well as hidden doors and corridors.\n\nnp_move_to - Move to the specified position using pathfinding.\n\nnp_go_to - Moves to the specified room or corridor using the shortest path possible.\n\nnp_press_key - Presses the given letter. For special keys only ESC, SPACE, and ENTER are supported.\n\nnp_type_text - Types the text by pressing the keys in order.\n\nreveal - Reveal a rectangular region of the dungeon map as ASCII (for the bounding-box observation mode, where the map is otherwise hidden). Coordinates are map cells: x = column 0-78, y = row 0-20, inclusive. The FULL map (x1=0, y1=0, x2=78, y2=20) is a valid request and returns all 79 columns. Returns the sub-rectangle as text; consumes NO game turn. Out-of-range requests are clamped to the grid, and any clamping is stated in the reply.\n\nrollback - Undo the last n turns, returning the game to the state it was in before them. Use after a mistake -- walking into a losing fight, triggering a trap, wasting turns in a dead end. Costs one turn and no game time. n must be between 1 and 15.\n\n",
        "name": "ipython"
