ast through the corridor at y7 to the far side of the level\n3. Navigate the corridor maze to reach (45,13)\n\nBut I can't use move_to because the pathfinder doesn't know the corridors. Let me try using type_text to move step by step. I can use the NetHack movement keys:\n- h = left (west)\n- j = down (south)\n- k = up (north)\n- l = right (east)\n- y = northwest\n- u = northeast\n- b = southwest\n- n = southeast\n\nFrom (10,4), I need to go to (8,6) to exit the room to the south. That's 2 steps west and 2 steps south. Let me type \"hhjj\" to move there. But actually, the room has walls, so I need to be careful about the exact path.\n\nLooking at the map:\n```\ny 4:      |....[.......|   #|...| #     |..........|     #########\ny 5:      |............|   #|...| #     ----.-+--+--       ------#\ny 6:      ---.----------   #----- #       ### #  #   ######.....|#\n```\n\nI'm at (10,4). To get to (8,6), I need to go:\n- From (10,4) to (10,5) - south (j)\n- From (10,5) to (8,5) - west (hh)\n- From (8,5) to (8,6) - south (j)\nThen from (8,6) to the corridor, go east.\n\nActually, let me just try to move to (8,6) first using the pathfinder - I know I can reach it since I was there before.",
