        "tool_call_id": "call_zxLMgM59bqjICedfCfkYwdAb",
        "content": "# hidden passage\n\nA hidden passage is a corridor or door that is not visible until searched. Many NetHack levels have hidden passages, especially the Gnomish Mines and dead-end corridors. To find them, stand adjacent to a suspected wall and call search repeatedly. Each search has roughly a 1/6 chance to reveal each hidden adjacent square, so 5-10 searches in one spot usually works.\n\nUse search(times=10) or search(times=20) to batch keystrokes. A hidden door shows as | or - in the wall; a hidden corridor shows as # in solid rock. Trapdoors and pit traps are also revealed by searching.\n\nTactics: when autoexplore reports no frontier and no > is visible, assume a hidden corridor or trapdoor. Walk to a dead-end and search 10-20 times. Mine Town and the Oracle level frequently have hidden passages.\n\n",
        "name": "ipython"
